id: pm-memory-quoted-credential-keys
title: Refuse quoted JSON and YAML credential keys before persistence
description: "Fix issue 52 in PR 51 at the shared privacy boundary. Refuse quoted JSON and YAML credential assignments before persistence or export, including normalized forms, while preserving environment and secret-manager references."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[2]: "gh:unbraind/pm-memory#52",privacy
created_at: "2026-11-06T14:53:38.758Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-14T10:12:38.896Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-14T08:57:58.702Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-13T10:13:34.000Z"
author: codex-sol
release: 2026.11.13
severity: high
comments[13]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-06T14:53:44.538Z",codex-sol,Discovered from review round 3 context on PR 51; issue 52 contains a synthetic real-tracker reproduction against main. This independent existing defect remains open and is not fixed by SDK adoption. Companion pm-cli-website-d8bz remains read only.
  "2026-11-06T16:31:13.834Z",codex-sol,"The orchestrator explicitly includes issue 52 in PR 51. Trace confirms remember checks privacy before schema and native writes, and export shares the same guard. Extend the narrowly documented generic assignment supplement for quoted keys; preserve SDK-owned provider rules, safe references and non-echoing errors. Verify genuine temporary SDK trackers and function-only reverts."
  "2026-11-06T16:55:16.779Z",codex-sol,"The reproduction now refuses before tracker mutation. Added nested JSON, JSON-serialized and escaped fragments, quoted YAML, normalized keys, malformed/over-budget encoding, SDK-short assignments, safe references, imported content and legacy export controls. The five regression cases and seven-case focused probe pass. Function-only reversions fail: original supplement 3 cases, original export 1 case, reference guard 1 case; disabling the baseline array guard fails its real-SDK control. Restoring the implementation passes all seven controls. The separate review pass added unterminated-literal coverage and preserved consent precedence and existing export email behavior. The security artifact helper is unavailable due to its Python dependencies; repository commands and PM/PR evidence are used, with no plugin artifact bundle claimed."
  "2026-11-06T17:09:15.602Z",codex-sol,"The separate representation review reproduced a second export route: a safe current body could still share a retained original document containing an encoded quoted credential. Added a genuine native-SDK legacy fixture and decoded-original preflight before publication; plaintext and known encoded source copies must satisfy the same credential guard. No credentials or tracker history are removed."
  "2026-11-06T17:26:56.460Z",codex-sol,"Final linked issue-52 regressions pass 6/6 with no skipped cases, including typed refusal before remember/import writes, non-echoing errors, normalized and nested copies, safe persisted/exported references, readable legacy bodies, and refusal of serialized original documents. Removing decoded-original inspection fails its new control; restoring it passes. The broader run executes 62 cases: 61 pass and the sole failure is the distinct-quote wall-time deadline under CPU contention. A subsequent linked deadline/JWT run passes all 6/6 at unchanged 500ms/process thresholds. Existing consent export refusal passes. Typecheck, lint, duplication 0 percent and docstrings pass. Closes #52 is prepared for PR 51; full exact-head CI and the queued review remain required."
  "2026-11-06T21:20:55.585Z",codex-sol,"Final combined issue-52 and round-5 secret controls pass 8/8 with no skips through the linked runner. Nested object and array descendants now inherit credential-key context, while explicit references remain readable and exportable. The inherited-context revert fails its regression; source restoration passes. The SDK finding policy uses its public literal union for exhaustive compile-time review, and unknown runtime findings refuse conservatively. Closes #52 remains in PR 51. Fresh CI is required after the final review fixes."
  "2026-11-09T18:25:28.652Z",pi-agent,"Round-11 fix (thread PRRT_kwDOVPw2oc61YZyq on the SDK adoption PR), class rule: a shape-based exemption in the credential fast path must be at least as strict as the documented safe set it carves out; content that does not match the documented shape must fall through to the full literal policy, never be blanket-accepted. Fixed instances of the class: (1) credentialLiteral exempted every /^<[^<>]*>$/ value, so a generic credential wrapped in angle brackets (a synthetic password literal in JSON) skipped the length rule and was stored; the exemption is now restricted to recognizable placeholder shapes (redacted, or letter-only words joined by spaces, underscores or hyphens). (2) The class search found the same bracket blindness in the free-text assignment rule: its assigned-value charset excludes angle brackets and the quoted-key signal path never sees unquoted keys, so free-text forms (colon or equals, quoted or bare) hid bracketed credentials entirely; a wrapper-aware scan now routes the bracketed value through the same credentialLiteral policy. Documented placeholder shapes (<redacted>, <secret-manager-reference>, letter-word phrases, uppercase) remain accepted; digits, symbols, provider tokens and credential material in brackets refuse; prose angle brackets without a credential key are unaffected. docs/sdk-adoption.md states the restricted placeholder contract."
  "2026-11-09T18:25:36.955Z",pi-agent,"Revert proofs in a disposable copy of the package worktree (behavioral reverts, implementation restored in the same copy afterwards): (1) reverting only the credentialLiteral placeholder restriction back to /^<[^<>]*>$/ fails the adversarial control (1 failure: the bracket-wrapped synthetic password is stored again through the JSON path); (2) removing only the free-text wrapper scan fails the same control (1 failure: the free-text colon/equals forms store the bracketed credential). Restoring each function passes the control again; no existing test was weakened or removed."
  "2026-11-09T18:36:32.875Z",pi-agent,"Round-11 final gates at the pushed head: all 4 linked tests pass through pm test --run --progress (including the combined quoted-credentials + sdk-adoption suite, 27/27 underlying cases; one earlier run of that combined entry hit its former 120s default timeout under host load and passes with a proper 600s window on retry). Wider focused suites pass: sdk-adoption + sdk-review-r4/r5/r6 + export-credential-original 33/33, memory + round2 + review-r1/r7 41/41. Typecheck, lint, docstring, duplication (0%, 0 clone pairs) and identity (0 violations) pass; the changelog is refreshed after these tracker writes. CI certifies the complete release gate."
  "2026-11-10T05:26:34.044Z",pi-agent,"Round-14 fix (thread PRRT_kwDOVPw2oc61eP9E, blocking). Class rule: a quote is surrounding syntax, never a reason to stop or exclude the interior of a recognized credential wrapper. Fixed instances: the free-text bracket scanner excluded quotes from the wrapper interior, so password assignments whose bracketed value contained a single or double quote were stored; the same scanner also required an unquoted key, so a quoted key with a quote inside the brackets truncated before the credential policy. Both now use one wrapper scan that keeps the full bracket interior and accepts a quoted key. The JSON scalar path already decoded internal quotes and was not a second implementation. The unquoted token scanner still stops at a quote because that quote starts another token and there is no wrapper to recover; that is a different rule. Markdown link parsing is not a credential scanner. Docs state the contract. Packed npm and bun consumers share this in-process scan."
  "2026-11-10T05:26:42.328Z",pi-agent,"Revert proofs in a disposable copy, restored afterwards: reverting only the bracket interior from any non-bracket character back to excluding quotes fails the quote-position control (1 failure: a quote inside the brackets is stored). Reverting only the quoted-key visibility fails the same control (1 failure: a quoted key whose bracketed value contains a quote is stored). Restoring the scanner passes the control. The control inserts each quote style at the start, middle and end of a credential and checks bare, equals, quoted-value and quoted-key forms, while recognized placeholders and prose quotes stay accepted."
  "2026-11-10T05:27:37.250Z",pi-agent,"Round-14 gates: the five linked tests pass through pm test --run, including the new quote-position control. Focused quoted-credentials suite passes 6/6. Typecheck, lint, docstring, duplication at 0 percent and identity with 0 violations pass. Changelog is refreshed after these tracker writes. CI certifies the full release gate."
  "2026-11-14T10:12:38.891Z",codex-sweep-1114,"Release-attribution correction: completed_at = 2026-11-13T10:13:34Z from https://github.com/unbraind/pm-memory/pull/51 (merge SHA d2d448e7e7b8372d1077b4c8d12d6f3ab5517920); first containing release tag v2026.11.13, recorded release 2026.11.13."
